('replace_p', 412, 2, "The discovery did not overturn genetics; it enlarged it. The genome is not a static text but one that contains instructions for editing itself. Most edits are harmless and a few are consequential, and the consequential ones are part of the history that produced the reader, whose genome still carries the editors."),
